  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 336 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nUpper level ridging and surface high pressure keeping dry conditions \naround through the end of the week and into next weekend. The main \nweather concern will be temperatures in the extended period. A \ngradual warming trend begins on Wednesday, although temperatures \nremain cool and well below normal on Wednesday. Expect highs to rise \ninto the mid 70s to low 80s. Highs will return to the 90s and low \n100s by Saturday lasting through early next week. There is some \nconcern that these highs have the potential to have widespread \ntemperatures over 100 degrees by the end of the weekend. Latest \nprobability forecasts show the potential of seeing over 100 degrees \nto be 40 to 50 percent for much of southwest Nebraska into the \nPanhandle. Elsewhere, probabilities are still near 30 percent \nfor much of the forecast area. At this time, while high \ntemperatures will be very hot, heat indicies will remain near or\nbelow 100 degrees. However, if this warming trend continues and\nconfidence increases over the next few days, heat headlines may\nbe necessary.",
